This product includes software developed by OpenMMLab, published as MMPose
(https://github.com/open-mmlab/mmpose, release v1.3.2) and described in "RTMO:
Towards High-Performance One-Stage Real-Time Multi-Person Pose Estimation"
(Lu, Jiang, Li, Li, Chen, Yang; CVPR 2024, arXiv:2312.07526).

The modules here are extracted from MMPose's RTMO implementation and from the
mmcv and mmengine building blocks it is assembled from (ConvModule, Swish,
MultiheadAttention, FFN, Scale). All three projects are licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0; see the LICENSE file in this directory, which is
the text MMPose publishes. The backbone is YOLOX's CSPDarknet and the neck is
RT-DETR's hybrid encoder, both as MMPose re-implements them.

The published checkpoints are taken to be Apache-2.0 as well. MMPose states no
separate terms for its model zoo, so this is an inference from the repository's
licence rather than a statement the authors make about the weights. They were
trained on "body7": COCO, AI Challenger, CrowdPose, MPII, sub-JHMDB, Halpe and
PoseTrack18, whose own terms govern those datasets.

The joint names in the published labels.json are COCO's own, from the
person_keypoints annotations (Creative Commons Attribution 4.0), and match the
checkpoints' own dataset metadata position by position.

NOT INCLUDED
------------
Training, the assigner, the losses, the proxy keypoint regression branch and
the MLE sigma branch are not part of this package; neither is mmdeploy's
switch_to_deploy re-parameterisation. See PROVENANCE.md for the full list and
for why.
